# What not to put in the .vsix.
#
# `vsce` ships the directory, so a file added here for maintainers is a file
# downloaded by everyone who installs the extension. `PUBLISHING.md` is about
# releasing this thing, which is nobody's business but ours; `README.md` stays,
# because it is what the Marketplace renders as the extension's page.
PUBLISHING.md
.vscodeignore
render-icon.sh
icon.svg

# **`.gitignore` does not apply here.** `vsce` packages the working directory,
# so a file kept out of the repository is still shipped to everyone who
# installs the extension unless it is named again in *this* file. `wrangler`
# leaves an account id and name in `.wrangler/cache/` after a deploy from this
# directory, and that went into a `.vsix` — the exact failure the note at the
# top of this file describes, by a route it did not anticipate.
.wrangler/

# A package should not contain the last one.
*.vsix
